Caelza: the two doors on quickstart's first screen (vision §3.4).

Caelza works with no account and no API key, and the first thing a new owner
sees should say so. The dashboard's Quickstart opened on a provider dropdown;
now its model-provider section opens on two doors. "Free and local" stages
the ladder's DeepSeek R1 for this device as `<runner>.local`, the alias
scripts/model-setup.sh and the app's first run write, with Cael's honest line
from the ladder (scripts/model_ladder.py); "Bring your own key" is upstream's
provider form as it was. The doors live in the overlay
(web/src/pages/quickstart/Doors.tsx, doors.logic.ts and its node test); these
hunks make the page render them, hoist the one stage callback both doors
share, name the door in the section's summary, add the strings (English; the
other locales fall back to it) and list the logic test beside upstream's.
Applied after 0006 and the overlay copy.

